@*
    The one mark that says "this sends your text to the language model".

    Asked for directly: the owner wanted to know, before pressing, which buttons
    produce an answer from the model and which are ordinary application actions.
    That distinction matters more here than in most software — an AI action costs
    money on the OpenAI account, takes seconds rather than milliseconds, can fail
    for reasons nothing else fails for, and returns a proposal that a person still
    has to check. None of that was visible on the button.

    It is deliberately one mark used in one meaning. The AI buttons previously
    carried ri-magic-line, ri-file-search-line or no icon at all, while ordinary
    buttons also carried icons, so nothing on the screen separated the two groups.
    A signal only works if it appears on every member of the set and on nothing
    else — which is what AiActionMarkingTests holds in place.
*@
